# KV cache — What is it?

KV cache is compressed (key-value) matrices standing for keys and values which are outputs of the Multi-head Attention layers.

# How does KV cache work?

Assume that our input sentence is: `I love coding`. At timestep 0, `I` (Inputs) will be matched with `<|endoftext|>` (keys of KV cache), resulting outputs as values of KV cache. These values are required to generate scores in the next timestep, 1.

