## Naive approach

One naive approach is to pre-fetch the weights data such that weights loading does not block computation (eventually leads to program halt). The idea is to use a separate thread to fetch the data while the model is serving requests. However, there are several problems with this approach:

- We will need to implement a caching layer for the weights data. Otherwise, the thread will need to read the disk multiple times, which is slow. But the implementation of the caching layer will depend on the storage medium, which is not ideal. For example, we may want to use mmap for disk storage and RDMA/Infiniband for network storage. Also, Disk is easier to handle than network storage as we do not need to worry about authentication/security.
- The solution only works for network storage (e.g. NFS, S3) or on-node disk storage (e.g. SSD). For off-node disk storage (e.g. Lustre), we may not be able to prefetch the data. Also, it is really hard to verify the effectiveness of the solution as we need to carefully design the experiment.

