With continuous bag-of-words representation, we concatenate all the word vectors into a single vector and feed the entire vector into a single hidden layer that allows the network to learn correlations and dependencies between various words in the sentence. This approach, while effective, has a significant limitation: the output depends on fixed-length context size (i.e., number of words in a given input sentence). It assumes that all the necessary context is present in the continuous bag of our words. Now, let’s build a more satisfying model!

