A checkpoint in Oracle Data Guard is a read-only copy of a completed transaction. A completed transaction is a transaction that was committed either on the primary database or on a logical standby database. However, the committed transactions on the standby database will be lost in case of failure.

Oracle Data Guard stores checkpoints in a standby redo log file. Standby redo log files are used during a role transition to a primary database (e.g., when the primary database is lost and the standby database takes over its place). During a role transition, Oracle Data Guard will scan the standby redo log for the last checkpoint for each thread. The oldest of them will determine the checkpoint SCR (System Change Number), used by Oracle to apply the redo data during recovery.
