🧠 LLM Response:

Speculative decoding helps in reducing the penalty cyles. For each data cache miss in a branch predictor, it usually takes us a lot of cycles for the target code of the branch instruction to be decoded. Speculative decoding allows the CPU to speculatively decode from multiple potential branch targets. When the branch target is finally setup, the CPU would had already finished with decoding. These decoded instructions are then issued.

Speculative decoding has a benefit known as indirect jump prediction. It predicts the destination for indirect jumps and then decodes the target code, thus nullifying the penalty of waiting for the cycle which would have added to the latency.
