## Components of Convolutional Neural Networks

A convolutional neural network (CNN) consists of layers of artificial neurons (which we will call nodes) that can extract features from incoming images.

The two main types of nodes in CNNs are:

- Convolution layer.
- Subsampling layer (also called pooling layer).

CNNs learn to extract higher and higher level features in deeper layers.

They can do this thanks to their unique architecture of alternating convolution and subsampling layers.

Now let’s explain this architecture in more detail.

## What is a Convolution Layer?

A Convolution Layer in a CNN is responsible for feature extraction from the input image.

A feature can be a horizontal or vertical line or an edge.

Nodes in a Convolution Layer perform computations in a very specific way.

The first layer of a CNN has its nodes arranged in a way that resembles the input image.

An Image is made of different pixels.

